---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CompressTool from '../components/CompressTool.astro';
const title = 'Compress Image to 30KB Online - Free | CompressImg';
const description = 'Reduce JPG, PNG and WebP images to 30KB or less in seconds. Free online compressor for profile pictures, ID photos and forms with tight upload size limits.';
const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'How to compress image to 30KB?',
    answer: 'Upload an image with the tool pre-set to 30KB. It optimizes the image, then adjusts JPEG quality and dimensions when needed so the download is at or below 30KB.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What dimensions work best for 30KB images?',
    answer: 'Images around 300x300 to 600x600 pixels usually retain better quality at 30KB. Larger images can work, but reaching the limit may require smaller dimensions and more visible compression.'
  }
];
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical="/compress-image-to-30kb" schemaType="WebApplication" faqItems={faqItems}>
      <section class="border-b border-stone-200 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-stone-200 bg-stone-100 px-3.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-stone-600">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent-500"></span>
        Compress to 30KB
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.08] tracking-tightest text-stone-900 md:text-5xl">Compress image to <span class="text-accent-700">30KB</span> online - free</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-[60ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 md:text-lg">Reduce your image to 30KB or less. Great for form submissions, small avatars, and websites with strict upload limits. Supports JPG, PNG, and WebP formats.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 -mt-2 mb-12">
    <CompressTool defaultTarget={30} showCustomTarget={true} />
  </section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900">Other compression sizes</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
      <a href="/compress-image-to-20kb" class="rounded-full border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-stone-600 transition duration-200 hover:border-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 active:scale-[0.97]">Compress to 20KB</a>
      <a href="/compress-image-to-50kb" class="rounded-full border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-stone-600 transition duration-200 hover:border-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 active:scale-[0.97]">Compress to 50KB</a>
      <a href="/compress-image-to-100kb" class="rounded-full border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-stone-600 transition duration-200 hover:border-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 active:scale-[0.97]">Compress to 100KB</a>
      <a href="/compress-image-to-200kb" class="rounded-full border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-stone-600 transition duration-200 hover:border-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 active:scale-[0.97]">Compress to 200KB</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900">Why Compress Images to 30KB?</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-600">The 30KB target sits in the sweet spot between the extremely restrictive 20KB limit and the more forgiving 50KB size. Many online portals, particularly in the education and government sectors, specify 30KB as their maximum upload size for photographs. This limit is common for student registration forms, examination applications, and employee profile uploads where systems need to handle large volumes of images efficiently.</p>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-600">At 30KB, you get noticeably better quality than at 20KB while still meeting strict upload requirements. Small avatars and profile pictures are particularly well-suited for 30KB compression since they're typically displayed at small sizes anyway. Forum avatars, comment profile pictures, and chat app display images all work well at this size.</p>
    <h2 class="mb-4 mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900">Optimizing Images for 30KB</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-600">To get the best results when compressing to 30KB, follow these guidelines. First, consider your image dimensions - images between 300x300 and 600x600 pixels work best at this file size. Very large images will be heavily compressed and may show artifacts. Second, images with solid color backgrounds compress better than those with busy, detailed backgrounds. If you're preparing a portrait or ID photo, a plain background will yield better results at 30KB.</p>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-600">Third, the subject matter matters. Images with lots of fine detail (hair, fur, complex patterns) will lose more detail at 30KB than simpler images. Our tool does its best to preserve important visual information by optimizing the quality dynamically. The intelligent compression algorithm iterates through quality levels to find the best possible result for your specific image at the 30KB target.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="border-t border-stone-200 bg-white py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="mb-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 md:text-3xl">Frequently Asked Questions - 30KB Compression</h2>
      <div class="divide-y divide-stone-200 border-y border-stone-200">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left text-[15px] font-medium text-stone-900 transition-colors hover:text-accent-700">
            How to compress image to 30KB?
            <svg class="faq-icon h-4 w-4 flex-shrink-0 text-stone-400 transition-transform duration-300 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.32,0.72,0,1)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-content hidden pb-5">
            <p class="max-w-[65ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600">Upload an image with the tool pre-set to 30KB. It optimizes the image, then adjusts JPEG quality and dimensions when needed so the download is at or below 30KB.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left text-[15px] font-medium text-stone-900 transition-colors hover:text-accent-700">
            What dimensions work best for 30KB images?
            <svg class="faq-icon h-4 w-4 flex-shrink-0 text-stone-400 transition-transform duration-300 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.32,0.72,0,1)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-content hidden pb-5">
            <p class="max-w-[65ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600">Images around 300x300 to 600x600 pixels usually retain better quality at 30KB. Larger images can work, but reaching the limit may require smaller dimensions and more visible compression.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-btn').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const content = btn.nextElementSibling;
      const icon = btn.querySelector('.faq-icon');
      content.classList.toggle('hidden');
      icon.classList.toggle('rotate-180');
    });
  });
</script>
